1
00:00:00,267 --> 00:00:01,447
Forty of them. One gate.

2
00:00:01,723 --> 00:00:03,013
He didn't look at me.

3
00:00:03,253 --> 00:00:04,553
He just stood there with

4
00:00:04,553 --> 00:00:05,793
his face against the
bars.

5
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:07,920
Then my radio crackled.

6
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,420
Is anyone still in the

7
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:09,660
mall?

8
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:11,760
I'm on the second floor

9
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:12,720
of the department store.

10
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:13,660
Please.

11
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:15,040
I'm not alone up here.

12
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:16,480
A woman. Whispering.

13
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:18,380
Somewhere upstairs in my
mall.

14
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:20,040
Her voice came out of

15
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:20,560
my radio.

16
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:22,280
And then, one second
later,

17
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:23,440
out of the radio on

18
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:24,280
Marcus's chest.

19
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:25,920
Every head in that
hallway

20
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:26,420
turned.

21
00:00:26,747 --> 00:00:28,387
They didn't run at it.

22
00:00:28,627 --> 00:00:30,767
They leaned on it, all

23
00:00:30,767 --> 00:00:31,907
at once, the way a

24
00:00:31,907 --> 00:00:33,127
crowd leans on the doors

25
00:00:33,127 --> 00:00:34,247
on Black Friday.

26
00:00:34,692 --> 00:00:35,807
And the steel started to

27
00:00:35,807 --> 00:00:36,027
bend.

28
00:00:36,515 --> 00:00:37,407
And she was about to

29
00:00:37,407 --> 00:00:37,807
call again.

30
00:00:39,197 --> 00:00:40,607
I switched my radio off.

31
00:00:40,867 --> 00:00:42,067
But his was still on.

32
00:00:42,407 --> 00:00:43,447
There was only one way

33
00:00:43,447 --> 00:00:44,587
to shut it up. I

34
00:00:44,587 --> 00:00:45,487
had to reach through the

35
00:00:45,487 --> 00:00:46,727
bars and take it off

36
00:00:46,727 --> 00:00:47,327
his chest.

37
00:00:47,787 --> 00:00:48,987
His teeth were about an

38
00:00:48,987 --> 00:00:50,187
inch from my wrist. The

39
00:00:50,187 --> 00:00:51,447
whole time, he was
looking

40
00:00:51,447 --> 00:00:52,267
right at me.

41
00:00:52,567 --> 00:00:53,667
And the clip stuck.

42
00:00:54,307 --> 00:00:55,947
He always wore it upside

43
00:00:55,947 --> 00:00:57,347
down. I must have told

44
00:00:57,347 --> 00:00:58,207
him a hundred times.

45
00:00:59,177 --> 00:01:00,567
I twisted it, and it

46
00:01:00,567 --> 00:01:01,067
came loose,

47
00:01:01,587 --> 00:01:02,407
and I fell back on

48
00:01:02,407 --> 00:01:03,167
the floor with it.

49
00:01:03,407 --> 00:01:04,467
I stuffed it as deep

50
00:01:04,467 --> 00:01:05,607
into a sleeping bag as

51
00:01:05,607 --> 00:01:06,087
it would go,

52
00:01:06,647 --> 00:01:07,727
and I lay there,

53
00:01:08,247 --> 00:01:08,867
not breathing.

54
00:01:09,387 --> 00:01:10,127
Without the noise,

55
00:01:10,567 --> 00:01:11,967
they forgot about me. It

56
00:01:11,967 --> 00:01:13,447
took maybe ten minutes.
One

57
00:01:13,447 --> 00:01:15,047
by one, they drifted back

58
00:01:15,047 --> 00:01:15,627
down the hall.

59
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:16,687
All except Marcus.

60
00:01:16,997 --> 00:01:19,307
Then, from inside the
sleeping

61
00:01:19,307 --> 00:01:20,787
bag, she said my name.

62
00:01:22,187 --> 00:01:23,527
When I grabbed that
radio,

63
00:01:24,107 --> 00:01:25,107
I must have squeezed the

64
00:01:25,107 --> 00:01:25,667
talk button.

65
00:01:26,147 --> 00:01:27,787
Danny, right? The night
guard.

66
00:01:28,107 --> 00:01:29,427
I can hear you breathing.

67
00:01:30,107 --> 00:01:32,187
She didn't sound scared
anymore.

68
00:01:32,727 --> 00:01:34,327
She sounded like someone
ordering

69
00:01:34,327 --> 00:01:34,907
a coffee.

70
00:01:35,387 --> 00:01:36,887
Don't worry. I'm not one

71
00:01:36,887 --> 00:01:37,227
of them.

72
00:01:37,807 --> 00:01:38,867
You've got all the keys,

73
00:01:39,087 --> 00:01:39,507
don't you?

74
00:01:40,317 --> 00:01:41,307
I didn't say a word.

75
00:01:41,907 --> 00:01:43,447
That's okay. Get some
sleep,

76
00:01:43,647 --> 00:01:44,667
Danny. We'll talk
tomorrow.

77
00:01:44,897 --> 00:01:47,107
Then the little light on

78
00:01:47,107 --> 00:01:47,887
the radio went out.

79
00:01:48,557 --> 00:01:49,327
I didn't sleep.

80
00:01:50,047 --> 00:01:51,127
I lay there and listened

81
00:01:51,127 --> 00:01:52,127
to Marcus lean on the

82
00:01:52,127 --> 00:01:53,487
gate every few minutes,
like

83
00:01:53,487 --> 00:01:54,227
he was checking that it

84
00:01:54,227 --> 00:01:54,887
was still locked.

85
00:01:55,327 --> 00:01:56,287
Here's what bothered me.

86
00:01:56,647 --> 00:01:57,847
The mall closes at nine.

87
00:01:58,307 --> 00:01:59,667
At midnight, I walked
every

88
00:01:59,667 --> 00:02:01,147
hallway and checked every
door,

89
00:02:01,307 --> 00:02:02,247
like I do every night.

90
00:02:02,647 --> 00:02:03,927
The department store was
locked.

91
00:02:04,227 --> 00:02:04,827
I locked it.

92
00:02:05,347 --> 00:02:06,187
Nobody was in here.

93
00:02:06,727 --> 00:02:08,027
So who was she? And

94
00:02:08,027 --> 00:02:08,847
what was she doing in

95
00:02:08,847 --> 00:02:09,907
my mall at two in

96
00:02:09,907 --> 00:02:10,227
the morning?
